{
 "format": "an.timing.easing",
 "version": 1,
 "description": "Every named easing, the solver that computes it, and its value at u = i/20. Hyphenated CSS names are the exact CSS curves; an's underscore names (and 'ease') are an's own polynomial curves; Manim's rate functions keep Manim's names. A bare 4-number list is a cubic Bezier solved by 'an-bezier-newton-8'; the string 'cubic-bezier(...)' is solved by 'css-bezier-newton-bisection'.",
 "families": [
  "common",
  "legacy",
  "css",
  "manim"
 ],
 "solvers": {
  "closed-form": "evaluated directly from its formula",
  "an-bezier-newton-8": "an's cubic Bézier: x(s) = t solved by exactly 8 Newton steps from s = t, each clamped to [0, 1], stopping only on a derivative below 1e-12; no bisection. Bit-identical to runtime.js cubicBezier",
  "css-bezier-newton-bisection": "the CSS cubic Bézier: up to 8 Newton steps from s = t (stop when |x(s) - t| < 1e-12, give up on a slope below 1e-6), then up to 60 bisection steps on [0, 1] to the same 1e-12",
  "css-steps": "the CSS Easing Level 1 step algorithm"
 },
